***********************************Interpretation for some parameters***********************************
#######################
input parameters
    9000     0   8000   ngrid_r0 lmin lmax
         ngrid_r0(ngrid_r in subroutine param_input) is the number of grids in the whole earth. The grids are equal-spacing. 
         To large extents, the accuracy of seismograms depend on this parameter. 

#######################
depth_cutoff is the depth used to determine the cut-off harmonic degree l. The current version cannot handle the case where the target 
depth is equal to the source depth.

#######################
In almost all subroutines, except param_input, ngrid_r represents the final number of radial grids. During source implementation, 
zero, one, or two additional nodes may be inserted. There are three possible cases (see line 229 in param.f):
1. The source is located between two grid nodes. Add one node with
  grid_r(itmp) = source_r
  (a) If the two nodes are the top nodes of a solid zone, add an additional node with
      r = ( grid_r(itmp) + source_r ) / 2.d0
  (b) Otherwise, do nothing.

2. The source is located exactly at the top node of a solid zone. Move the source slightly deeper and add two nodes.

3. All other cases. Do nothing. For example, if the source is located exactly on a grid node below the top node, no additional nodes are inserted.

########################
Maximum number of radial nodes

The maximum number of radial nodes is fixed and equally spaced. Every 100 harmonic-degree (l) iterations, the subroutine check_amp_significance 
is called to update the cut-off radius and determine whether the computation should terminate.
########################
idim1_sph, idim0, idim1_sph0, and idim2_sph in comp_wavefield
idim1_sph = max0( idim0,idim1_sph0 )
idim0 is updated every 100 harmonic-degree iterations in check_amp_significance.
idim1_sph0 = 1 and idim2_sph = ngrid_r are fixed after the radial grids are generated.

These variables define the deepest grid point (minimum ir) to which the equations are solved. In check_amp_significance,

if(itmp.gt.min_ir_dep) itmp=min_ir_dep

ensures that the solution always extends at least to the deepest station.
