***************************Solving the linear equations Ax=B***************************************************
All modes with different m values (from -2 to 2) but the same harmonic degree l share the same coefficient matrix A. Therefore, the Cholesky 
decomposition of A only needs to be performed once (for example, for m=−2 in the moment-tensor case). The remaining m values are obtained by forward substitution.

Wenbo Wu modified the code so that the linear system includes all station grids, even when their amplitudes fall below the threshold (eps in check_amp_significance). Otherwise, solutions would not be available at those stations.

